2026-10-02T16:59:43.4492651Z   ok   the inferred estimator reads a real defrost as a PERFECT interval
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4493113Z   ok   an over-1 ratio can no longer park the derate above 1.0
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4493517Z   ok   five defrosting minutes in thirty is a duty of 1/6
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4493872Z   ok   and the interval counts as observed
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4494339Z   ok   a quiet interval is duty zero AND observed — that is real evidence
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4495321Z   ok   an unreadable flag yields duty zero but NOT observed
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4495880Z   ok   a defrost spanning an interval boundary keeps its second half
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4496358Z   ok   a sample stamped before the last does not subtract from the on-time
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4496756Z   ok   zero duty is no derate at all
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4497083Z   ok   the derate is 1 - duty x the loss multiplier
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4497503Z   ok   more duty is always a deeper derate, never a shallower one
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4497953Z   ok   and it is bounded below, so a latched flag cannot zero the pump
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4498374Z   ok   a measured bucket derates from its counted duty
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4498828Z   ok   and a measurement is never averaged with an inference of the same thing
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4499274Z   ok   an untouched bucket still derates nothing
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4499810Z   ok   the summary says which estimator a bucket rests on, and how many defrosts were actually witnessed
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4500380Z   ok   a duty outside [0, 1] is refused, not folded into the bucket
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4500907Z   ok   the range guard rejects only OUTSIDE [0, 1] — 0 and 1 still fold
2026-10-02T16:59:43.4501389Z   ok   a pre-v5.3.0 store loads without raising, and says it was upgraded
