2026-10-02T17:01:32.6186070Z   ok   observe mode (the default) refuses to turn the switch on
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6186540Z   ok   control mode with no switch refuses to write, and reads no state at all
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6187048Z   ok   ON while the pump's mode blocks hot water is refused, and logged once
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6187578Z   ok   a successful ON writes once, the memo stops the repeat, and the switch is owned
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6188049Z   ok   a switch already on is not written and not claimed
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6188526Z   ok   a write that raises warns, returns False and records neither memo nor ownership
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6189130Z   ok   …so the next call retries the write, and success clears the failure
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6189656Z   ok   every write asks Home Assistant to block until the service call has finished
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6190316Z   ok   a write that does not finish within the timeout is a failed write: no memo, no ownership, retried next cycle
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6190904Z   ok   the write timeout is bounded well inside one update cycle
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6191510Z   ok   control for the test registry: a rejected write raises only for blocking=True, as in Home Assistant core
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6192163Z   ok   a switch with no state is not written, is not a failed write, and is not claimed
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6192752Z   ok   …and an unload keeps the record of an owned switch that has no state
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6193272Z   ok   an accepted ON that does not read back on is a failed write with no ownership
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6193827Z   ok   …and an unload OFF that does not read back off keeps the record
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6194837Z   ok   control for the test registry: a blocking call to an id with no state returns without raising and without reaching a handler, as in booted core
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6195652Z   ok   release writes nothing for a switch that is not owned, even one that reads on
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6196347Z   ok   release of the configured owned switch: unavailable waits, on writes OFF, off ends ownership without a write
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6197013Z   ok   the configured owned switch, unavailable past the grace, is still waited for
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6197756Z   ok   an owned switch that is no longer configured and cannot be read is kept through the grace, then dropped into lost with no write
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6198434Z   ok   the grace the repair's text calls half an hour is thirty minutes
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6199079Z   ok   a blind release (unload) writes OFF to every owned switch unread, and keeps only the record whose OFF failed
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6199854Z   ok   control: the boost-start edge turns the switch ON exactly once across three commanded cycles, and owns it
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6200703Z   ok   …and the ownership is in the cycle's store, where a restart reads it
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6201350Z   ok   …and the boost close turns it OFF exactly once, and ownership ends when it reads off
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6202141Z   ok   with the optimizer off a legionella action still current never turns the disinfection switch on (null control above: on, it does)
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6202827Z   ok   the boost bound closes the window and turns the switch OFF once
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6203303Z   ok   a boost the bound closed is not switched back on by the same command
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6203860Z   ok   …and once the plan has moved on, the next commanded boost turns it on
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6204332Z   ok   disabling disinfection during a boost turns the switch OFF
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6205048Z   ok   no ON while this cycle's mode reading blocks hot water, logged once
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6205683Z   ok   …and the ON goes out on the first cycle the mode allows hot water, with no solve between
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6206448Z   ok   a switch that was already on is left alone through a whole boost and after it
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6206928Z   ok   an idle control install writes nothing, not even OFF
2026-10-02T17:01:32.6207361Z   ok   a failed write raises a non-persistent repair naming the switch
